   "from_schema": 2,
   "harm": "delegating template eviction responsibility to the client can cause out of memory crashes if handled poorly",
   "hash": "3753921b35c03023",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-24T23:12:57+00:00",
     "by": "run:20260924-2308",
     "cause": "c:3564018931",
     "clears_with": "answer",
     "status": "answered",
     "type": "objection"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:3564018931",
   "kind": "approach",
   "other_replies": [],
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "Delegating template eviction responsibility to the client can put us in a situation where they handle it poorly and cause us to OOM",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2025-11-24",
    "by": "Sjors",
    "id": "c:3570105870",
    "quote": "In the scenario where they handle it poorly, we can use FIFO deletion. All `getMemoryLoad()` does is give clients an opp"
   },
   "status_note": "author explained client responsibility is inherent to multiprocess and FIFO eviction can be used as a fallback if needed",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33922#issuecomment-3564018931"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-11-21",
   "author": "ismaelsadeeq",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:3563799563"
   ],
   "clears_with": "answer",
   "fix": null,
   "from_schema": 2,
   "harm": "use internal memory management with a memory budget and FIFO template release rather than relying on IPC clients",
   "hash": "21281572c8b93bab",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T04:00:36+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "r:3493499544",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "r:3493499544",
   "kind": "approach",
   "other_replies": [],
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "In my opinion, we should not rely on the IPC client to manage our memory.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2025-11-21",
    "by": "Sjors",
    "id": "c:3563799563",
    "quote": "It seems counter intuitive, but from a memory management perspective IPC clients are treated no different than our own c"
   },
   "status_note": "author explained internal memory management treats IPC clients no differently than internal code, and FIFO eviction can be a last resort",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33922#pullrequestreview-3493499544"
  },
  {
